L2:(3) The head of the local CAO, or designee, will approve the annual cost monitoring plan within 15 days of an adequate submission. The head of the local CAO will ensure that adequate coordination of the cost monitoring plan was performed with the DCAA and other responsible Government representatives.
L4:(D) Perform functional reviews and audits as scheduled in accordance with the cost monitoring plan.
L2:(1) Hold interim meetings with the contractor as necessary to clarify information. Hold an exit conference at the conclusion of reviews.
L2:(2) Prepare reports at the conclusion of reviews. The ACO will determine whether a Government review or audit report will be provided to a contractor based on specific regulatory requirements or the impact to pending negotiations or litigation.
L2:(3) Prepare periodic reports on the results of the CMS analysis and monitoring of the contractors rates and factors, which should address the causes for significant deviations from historical and negotiated forward pricing rates and factors.
L4:(E) Prepare an annual cost monitoring report which is a culmination of the Government activities performed during the fiscal year in an effort to conduct and maintain a formal monitoring program of contractor policies, procedures, and practices for controlling costs charged to Government contracts. The report should—
L2:(1) Provide a brief introduction of the contractor and the products it provides to the Government;
L2:(2) Summarize each review and audit completed during the reporting period along with any deviations from the cost monitoring plan;
L2:(3) Highlight open deficiencies, corrected deficiencies, and any newly reported deficiencies; and
L2:(4) Include the current status of all final, billing, and forward pricing rates.
L2:(5) Incorporate the final DCAA audit reports by summary and reference.
L4:(F) (1) The head of the local CAO, or designee, will approve the annual cost monitoring report within 60 days of the end of the Government fiscal year.
L2:(2) Provide a copy of the approved report to the head of the local DCAA office within 15 days of approval.

